On Sat, 8 Nov 2003, Gregory M. Nosch wrote:

> I recently got a AlphaPC 164SX motherboard with 533mhz
> processor. I have spent many hours trying to install
> OpenBSD on it. I have read(and re-read) the install notes
> and pounded google for help. I know that there is some
> possible instability with my hardware(random hangs and
> crashes). I basically want to know if I am not doing
> something right or is my hardware unsupported.

buying an AlphaPC *164* class system is a crapshoot.  I think saying there
is possible instability should be rephrased as possible stability.  I
support 5 "Digital AlphaPC 164LX 533 MHz" systems that I recommended to a
friend/customer to buy before I'd read the OBSD Alpha page thoroughly.
Some of them run for months with no problems, other's failed soon after I
got them, they seem to be VERY picky about memory.  Also as noted in the
list there may be issue with IDE.  A system that had been up for 5 months
just panic'd, I believe when it was in the process of rolling logs.  I've
purchased a supported SCSI controller to see if it helps.

I feel so bad about recommending these systems to a small business that
I'm puchasing, at my expense, a Sparc U2 to put in place of their primary
Alpha system.  I check the Alpha systems at least twice a day 'cause I
don't feel comfortable with them.

I doubt you wanted to hear this.

g.day

